Z||000004||beer_stud_21||11-20-2001||06:52 PM||||Darwin the (open source) Unix core of OS X will run on X86, but Apple hasn't released the rest of OS X for X86.  There has been rumors for a long time that apple has been quietly keeping a X86 version of OS X in the wings.  But who knows when they will or if they will ever release it.  With the talk about the new PPC chips G5, G6, etc looking good <B>finally</B> I highly doubt if they will ever release it.  The G5 chip is looking like it will be awsome while the new intel chips arn't so hot.  The P4 is a Mhz monster (while giving lackluster performance per Mhz) but intels next chips are not able to keep up so it looks like intel will be taking hit Mhz wise.  They are going to have to eat their own words when it comes to the Mhz myth.  <P>As for using OS X.  I havn't had the chance yet.  I bought a beige G3 off of ebay recently but it hasn't gotten here yet.  As soon as it gets here I'm going to install OS X.  Then my first programming project is going to be a Cocoa version of PIP.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>The three CD's were OS X 10.04, OS X 10.1 update, and OS 9.2.  No 10.1 Dev Tools unless it might be in with the 10.1 update.  I will have to check.<P>-Marlin||||reg||1
